# Empyralis operator console (Next.js production server) -- a SECOND,
# independent Node process from empyralis-frontend.service, on its own port.
# Modeled directly on deploy/empyralis-frontend.service's shape (same
# User=empyralis, same `npm run start` ExecStart, same Restart policy) --
# see that file's own header for the reasoning behind each choice this unit
# copies. Differences from that file, and why:
#
#   - WorkingDirectory/PORT point at this app's own checkout and port
#     (3100, not 3000) -- it is a completely separate application per the
#     founder's explicit instruction, not a second route tree inside the
#     customer frontend. The production box has ~1GB RAM free; this is a
#     second small Next process, not a duplicate of the customer app's own
#     (no lucide-react/motion, no fleet-theme.css, no chat/board/agent-
#     detail routes -- see ops/next.config.ts and ops/package.json).
#   - EMPYRALIS_API_URL is the SAME backend both processes talk to
#     (127.0.0.1:8001) -- this app reads server_modules/routes_operator_
#     console.py through its own ops/lib/server/operator-proxy.ts, which
#     forwards the browser's session cookie server-side exactly the way
#     frontend/lib/server/control-plane-proxy.ts already does.
#
# BEFORE this unit's app can actually show data to a signed-in operator,
# TWO things need to be true on the box (outside this file's control):
#
#   1. The backend's `FRONTEND_ORIGINS` env var (deploy/empyralis-backend
#      .service or /root/pm2-env.sh -- see CLAUDE.md: "production never
#      loads .env") must include https://ops.empyralis.ai, or CORS-adjacent
#      backend checks that key off it may reject requests server_modules/
#      auth.py doesn't already treat as same-origin. server-to-server calls
#      from this app's own Next process are not subject to browser CORS, but
#      any check that reads FRONTEND_ORIGINS directly still needs the entry.
#   2. The backend's `EMPYRALIS_AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN` (server_modules/auth.py
#      _cookie_domain()) must be the shared PARENT domain (e.g.
#      `.empyralis.ai`), not left unset/scoped to empyralis.ai alone -- a
#      cookie set for one subdomain is never sent to a sibling subdomain by
#      the browser. This is the actual mechanism behind "reuse the
#      platform's existing session": the SAME empyralis_access_token /
#      empyralis_refresh_token / empyralis_csrf_token cookies the customer
#      app's login already issues have to reach ops.empyralis.ai too. If
#      this is not already how the box is configured, an operator visiting
#      ops.empyralis.ai for the first time will need to sign in there
#      separately (server_modules/routes_auth.py's own /login already works
#      standalone) -- the console still works, sessions just don't carry
#      over automatically until this is set.
#
# Install: copy to /etc/systemd/system/empyralis-ops.service,
# `systemctl daemon-reload`, `systemctl enable --now empyralis-ops`.
# Deploy the app itself the same way frontend/ is deployed -- `npm install`
# then `npm run build` in ops/, from a checkout at the WorkingDirectory path
# below (a detached/nohup'd build, per docs/DEPLOY-RUNBOOK.md's own note
# that a dropped SSH session kills an attached frontend build).

[Unit]
Description=Empyralis Operator Console (Next.js)
After=network.target empyralis-backend.service
Wants=empyralis-backend.service

[Service]
Type=simple
User=empyralis
Group=empyralis
WorkingDirectory=/opt/empyralis-app/ops
ExecStart=/usr/bin/npm run start
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5
Environment=NODE_ENV=production
Environment=PORT=3100
Environment=EMPYRALIS_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
SyslogIdentifier=empyralis-ops

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
